{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>לאדרכונים</b> (to the adarkhonim): the alef is superfluous, and it is like the sense of darkhonim. For the pattern adarkhonim, they are a thousand." "<b>וכלי נחשת מצהב</b> (and bronze vessels glowing gold): like the sense of 'polished, glowing gold' — once masculine and once feminine, as in the case of 'וְרוּחַ גְּדוֹלָה וְחָזָק' (a great and strong wind), and likewise 'שְׁנַיִם חֲמוּדוֹת' (two desirable ones)."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The final clause 'הם אלף' is obscure; translated hyper-literally. Possibly 'they are one thousand' referring to the quantity, or a statement about the numerical value or weight."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:21.042224265Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}